<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco lifts bunker fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco lifts bunker fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has increased A-960 bunker oil from Ras Tanura and Dammam by $3 to $104 a tonne ($15.97 a barrel) effective February 20, it said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel is also increased by $3 to $214  from the Gulf and $203 from Jeddah and Yanbu on the Red Sea.</p>
<p>A-960 from Red Sea ports is hiked by $4 to $107 ($16.43).</p>
</text>
